      "message": "Minor (P3): int() silently truncates a fractional ssm_default_lifetime, which pre-fix worked. YAML \"1.5\" -\u003e float 1.5 -\u003e int(1.5) \u003d\u003d 1. Pre-fix, a float lifetime was supported end to end (days_ahead \u003c 1.5 and timedelta(days\u003d1.5) \u003d\u003e 36h); post-fix the branch selection at line 273 changes (days_ahead\u003d1: 1 \u003c 1.5 was True -\u003e deadline-window path, now 1 \u003c 1 is False -\u003e start + 1 day, so end lands after the 21:00 deadline) and the duration becomes 24h. selfservice.yml documents the value \"in days\" without excluding fractions; the shipped value (5) is an int. If fractions are unsupported, reject non-integers with a 400; otherwise keep the float. (The malformed-string case, ValueError -\u003e 500, equals the pre-fix TypeError class and is lower priority.)",
