      "side": 1,
      "message": "Semantics/question (P2 for weekday-deadline configs): this fallback also catches negative days_ahead, not just the issue\u0027s days_ahead\u003d\u003d0 case. When the configured ssm_deadline_day (:13 selfservice.yml, configurable) has a weekday index below today\u0027s, days_ahead \u003d target_day - current_day is negative: pre-fix those requests were rejected with 400 \"Invalid date range\"; post-fix they now pass with end \u003d start + ssm_default_lifetime, even when the NEXT deadline window falls inside the lifetime. docs/quads-self-schedule.md:94 says the end date is \"the next ssm_deadline_day/ssm_deadline_hour window if it falls within ssm_default_lifetime days\". Probe (patch applied): deadline\u003dWed 21:00, now\u003dSun 20:00, lifetime\u003d5 -\u003e days_ahead\u003d-4 -\u003e end \u003d Fri 20:00, while the next deadline is Wed 21:00 (3 days away) and should be used per the docs. Not a regression (pre-fix always rejected) and unreachable with the shipped sunday default, but the fix is incomplete for weekday deadlines. Suggest days_ahead \u003d (target_day - current_day) % 7 so the window branch picks the NEXT deadline, keeping this fallback for the same-day post-deadline case, plus a test with a weekday deadline.",
